    "adm.nosql": "The admin functions are not installed on the server yet: open Supabase → SQL Editor and run the \"admin mode\" part at the end of supabase/schema.sql",
    "mq.pop100.h": "Build roads, then zone residential next to them. You need both a power plant and a water plant (near a river/sea) for homes to grow",
    "mq.pop500.h": "Zone more housing. Double-click a house to upgrade it to a townhouse/apartment (needs the city level). Parks and schools nearby make homes grow faster",
    "mq.pop1500.h": "Upgrade homes to apartments/condos, provide enough jobs (commercial/industrial) and keep power & water sufficient (no red numbers in the top bar)",
    "mq.lv3.h": "Needs 600 population, 8 days of city age, 50%+ happiness, enough power & water, and a school. Check the requirements on the level badge by the city name",
    "mq.fish.h": "Pick the \"Farm\" tool (key 0), hover the button and choose \"Fish farm\". Place it on a free 3×2 area (no road needed). Unlocks at city level 2",
    "mq.cricket.h": "Pick the \"Farm\" tool (key 0), hover the button and choose \"Cricket farm\". Place it on a free 2×2 area. Cheap and available from level 1",
    "mq.farms4.h": "Pick the \"Farm\" tool (key 0) and place any 4 farms: rice, vegetables, orchard, fish... (they need water and power)",
    "mq.services.h": "In the \"Service\" menu place one school, hospital, police station and fire station (hospital, police and fire unlock at level 2)",
    "mq.parks10.h": "Pick the \"Park\" tool and place several. Bigger parks give more tiles, e.g. a 2×2 plaza = 4 tiles. Parks also make nearby homes grow faster",
    "mq.transit.h": "In the \"Service\" menu build a bus depot (level 3) or metro station (level 4) near housing; add taxi/Grab depots and a car park next to metro stations for park & ride. Cheap fares and pricey parking push more people onto transit",
    "mq.export.h": "Build a freight terminal (\"Service\" menu, level 3) and make farms/factories produce a surplus. What the city does not use is exported automatically. See the \"Trade\" tab in the population panel",
    "mq.rich.h": "Keep daily net income positive: fill zones with homes and shops, add factories and exports, and avoid unnecessary buildings. Check income and expenses on the money card at the top",
    "mq.how": "💡 How to",
